%% repo-wrap
%% Summary: Resolve and classify one target, execute its ownership rail, and reconcile only proven-redundant build worktrees after a complete owned-project closeout.
%% Sources: skills/repo-wrap/core.md
%% Not shown: owner-match algorithm, secrets patterns, worktree proof commands, per-rail Git commands, backup naming, flags, maintenance procedure, and final report fields
%% Alt: A closeout router classifies one target and follows its ownership rail; after a complete owned-project closeout it removes only stale, clean build worktrees whose committed content is already shipped.

flowchart TD
    A[Resolve exactly one target] --> B[Classify ownership and workspace location]
    B --> C{Classification}
    C -- Registered project --> D[Delegate to project closeout]
    C -- Coding root --> E[Screen additions; park anomalies and suspects]
    C -- Clone --> F[Screen staged paths; protect upstream]
    C -- Other --> G[Screen paths; guard repo creation]
    E --> I[Commit safe snapshot; push only to owner]
    F --> J[Commit locally; push only to owned remote]
    G --> K[Back up safely or print guarded commands]
    D --> H{Closeout complete?}
    H -- Yes --> L[Reconcile proven-redundant build worktrees]
    H -- No --> R[Report delegated result]
    L --> R
    I --> R
    J --> R
    K --> R
